    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Remove keyframe point(s) from a segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type(s): video, audio, text, sticker\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --animated-property TEXT \r\n                              Animated property to remove: position-x, position-y, scale,\r\n                              scale-x, scale-y, rotation, opacity, or volume\r\n          --keyframe-type, --type TEXT \r\n                              Advanced escape hatch: exact case-sensitive KFType* constant\r\n          --time, --times <duration-list> \r\n                              Timestamp(s) to remove, requires an animated property (e.g. 1s or\r\n                              1s,2s). Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers\r\n                              and m are invalid.\r\n          --indexes TEXT      Csv group-local keyframe indexes to remove, requires an animated\r\n                              property (e.g. 0,2). Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --timeline-index TEXT \r\n                              Csv timeline keyframe indexes to remove (e.g. 0,1). Unitless\r\n                              whole-number index.\r\n          --all               Remove all keyframes from the target segment\r\n          --material-id TEXT  Material id for per-material keyframes (mask/HSL/effect slider)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Remove alpha keyframes at 1s and 2s\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft keyframe remove --seg-id <UUID> --animated-property opacity --times 1s,2s\r\n  # Remove all keyframes on the segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft keyframe remove --seg-id <UUID> --all\r\n",
